# Dawnhand Dissident's permission to cast from exile is a static ability (CR 604.1): a Dissident that has lost all its abilities
# (CR 613.1f) gives none. Bot1 exiles Llanowar Elves with the Dissident, then Abigale, Eloquent First-Year's entering ability makes
# the Dissident lose all abilities and puts three keyword counters on it. With six counters among Bot1's creatures and {G} open, the
# Elves can't be cast from exile. The twin, where Abigale's ability goes on the Sylvan Caryatid instead and the Elves are cast, is
# "...removes-counters-of-any-kinds-naming-which-from-a-creature-with-several".

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Dawnhand Dissident
Forest
Mox Emerald
Sylvan Caryatid
Abigale, Eloquent First-Year
Plains
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Forest x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dawnhand Dissident.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sylvan Caryatid.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Dawnhand Dissident.Activate(Ability: Surveil)
Bot1.Choose(Tap Dawnhand Dissident)
Bot1.Choose(Dawnhand Dissident)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Arrange( | Llanowar Elves)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Dawnhand Dissident.Activate(Bot1.Graveyard.Llanowar Elves; Ability: Exile target)
Bot1.Choose(Tap Dawnhand Dissident)
Bot1.Choose(Sylvan Caryatid)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Abigale, Eloquent First-Year.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Target(Dawnhand Dissident)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest#2.Activate
! Bot1.Exile.Llanowar Elves.Cast

[Expect]
Exile = Llanowar Elves
Bot1.Battlefield.Dawnhand Dissident.Counters.Flying = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Dawnhand Dissident.Counters.MinusOneMinusOne = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Sylvan Caryatid.Counters.MinusOneMinusOne = 2
